---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import EmhLab from "../../components/EmhLab.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Can You Beat the Market?"
  description="An efficient-markets game: predict a stock's next move and discover you're at coin-flip odds — and that trying to time the market usually trails just holding."
>
  <section class="container emh-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>Can you beat the market?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A stock chart is unfolding. You can see its whole history — the trend, the
      dips, the "momentum." All you have to do is call the next move: up or down.
      Simple, right? Play a few rounds and watch what happens to your score.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container emh-host">
    <EmhLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container emh-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why you can't win</h2>
      <p>
        This chart is a simulated random walk — but that's exactly the point:
        <strong>real stock charts are nearly indistinguishable from random ones.</strong>
        The trends and patterns your eye finds are mostly illusions in noise. If
        the past reliably predicted the future, everyone would trade on it, and
        the pattern would vanish the instant it appeared. So your accuracy sits
        near <strong>50%</strong> — a coin flip.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's the <strong>Efficient Markets Hypothesis</strong>: prices already
        reflect the available information, so you can't systematically beat them.
        Economists sort it into three strengths:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Weak form</strong> — prices already reflect all <em>past prices</em>, so chart-reading (technical analysis) can't give an edge. That's the game above.</li>
        <li><strong>Semi-strong form</strong> — prices reflect all <em>public information</em>. By the time you read the news (📰 flags above), the price has already jumped. You can't profit from it.</li>
        <li><strong>Strong form</strong> — prices reflect <em>even private information</em>. The strongest claim, and the most debated.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        And notice the second scoreboard: jumping in and out ("timing the market")
        usually <em>trails</em> simply holding, because you inevitably sit out some
        of the market's biggest up-days — which arrive unpredictably. That's the
        practical punchline, and it rhymes with the
        <a href="/tools/superstocks">superstock problem</a>: the case for owning
        the whole market and staying put.
      </p>
      <p>
        Markets aren't <em>perfectly</em> efficient — mispricings exist, and a few
        investors genuinely exploit them. But it's far harder than it looks, which
        is the honest lesson here. Educational only, not advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextTool current="/tools/beat-the-market" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .emh-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .emh-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .emh {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  @media (min-width: 940px) {
    .emh {
      grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
  .emh-chart-wrap {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .emh-controls {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .emh-prompt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .emh-btn {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.5rem 1.3rem;
    border: var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-text);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: transform var(--transition), border-color var(--transition);
  }
  .emh-btn:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .emh-btn--up:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .emh-btn--down:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-error);
    color: var(--color-error);
  }
  .emh-btn--new {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-accent-contrast);
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .emh-side {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .emh-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .emh-stats > div {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .emh-stats dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .emh-stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .emh-acc {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .emh-good {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .emh-bad {
    color: var(--color-error);
  }
  .emh-verdict {
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-md);
  }
  .emh-verdict p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .emh-verdict p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .emh-verdict-head {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
  }
  .emh-hint {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .emh-cumulative {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding-top: var(--space-sm);
    border-top: var(--border);
  }
  .emh-cum-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .emh-cum-bar {
    position: relative;
    height: 0.7rem;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: 999px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .emh-cum-fill {
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: 999px;
    transition: width var(--transition);
  }
  .emh-cum-mid {
    position: absolute;
    top: -2px;
    bottom: -2px;
    left: 50%;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--color-text);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  .emh-cum-val {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
</style>
